  "description": "Florida's 17th Congressional District, covering parts of Sarasota, Charlotte, and Lee Counties along the southwest Gulf Coast, is holding its regularly scheduled election for the U.S. House of Representatives in 2026. Incumbent Republican Greg Steube, first elected in 2018, is seeking a fifth term in a district rated 'Solid R' by the Cook Political Report. Two Democrats\u2014Matthew Montavon and Allen Spence\u2014are competing in the August 18 Democratic primary to challenge Steube, while Michael Quirk is running as a No Party Affiliation candidate in the general election. The race takes place under a new congressional map signed into law in May 2026 that could shift the partisan balance of several Florida districts.",
